Memo view visibility is enforced in **multiple independent server surfaces**, with several separate implementations inside the API v1 layer. The store layer only applies `VisibilityList` / `MemoFilter` when callers pass them—it does not autonomously enforce access.

---

## Visibility model (shared semantics)

| Level | Who may view |
|-------|----------------|
| **PUBLIC** | Anyone (anonymous allowed on some surfaces if the instance permits it) |
| **PROTECTED** | Authenticated users only |
| **PRIVATE** | Memo creator only (admins/super-users get extra access on some paths) |

---

## 1. API v1 — Connect / gRPC-Gateway (`/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/`)

Primary RPC surface. Visibility is **not centralized**; multiple handlers enforce it independently.

### 1a. Memo read gate — `memo_service.go`

```39:67:/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
func (s *APIV1Service) checkMemoReadAccess(ctx context.Context, memo *store.Memo) error {
	// ...
	// Archived memos are only visible to their creator.
	// ...
	if memo.Visibility != store.Public {
		// requires auth; PRIVATE denied unless creator
	}
}
```

Used by `GetMemo` (and parent memo), `ListMemoComments` (parent memo).

### 1b. Memo list scoping — `memo_service.go`

```218:227:/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go
	if currentUser == nil {
		memoFind.VisibilityList = []store.Visibility{store.Public}
	} else {
		if memoFind.CreatorID == nil {
			filter := fmt.Sprintf(`creator_id == %d || visibility in ["PUBLIC", "PROTECTED"]`, currentUser.ID)
			memoFind.Filters = append(memoFind.Filters, filter)
		} else if *memoFind.CreatorID != currentUser.ID {
			memoFind.VisibilityList = []store.Visibility{store.Public, store.Protected}
		}
	}
```

`ListMemos` pre-filters at query time (anonymous → PUBLIC only; viewing another user → PUBLIC+PROTECTED).

### 1c. Attachment metadata — `attachment_service.go`

```422:454:/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/attachment_service.go
func (s *APIV1Service) checkAttachmentAccess(ctx context.Context, attachment *store.Attachment) error {
	// unlinked → creator only
	// linked → follows parent memo visibility (PUBLIC open; PROTECTED needs auth; PRIVATE needs creator/super-user)
}
```

Used by `GetAttachment`.

### 1d. Reactions — `reaction_service.go`

Inline checks in `ListMemoReactions` / `UpsertMemoReaction`: non-PUBLIC requires auth; PRIVATE requires creator or super-user.

### 1e. Memo attachments list — `memo_attachment_service.go`

Inline check in `ListMemoAttachments` (same PUBLIC / auth / PRIVATE-creator pattern as reactions).

### 1f. Comments — `memo_service_comments.go`

- `CreateMemoComment`: blocks PRIVATE memos unless creator/super-user.
- `ListMemoComments`: `checkMemoReadAccess` on parent + `memoFilter` on comment memos (`visibility == "PUBLIC"` or creator/PUBLIC+PROTECTED).

### 1g. Relations — `memo_relation_service.go` + `memo_service_converter.go`

Both build the same CEL `memoFilter` and pass it to `Store.ListMemoRelations` so related memos the caller cannot view are excluded:

- Anonymous: `visibility == "PUBLIC"`
- Authenticated: `creator_id == {user} || visibility in ["PUBLIC", "PROTECTED"]`

Sites: `ListMemoRelations` (`memo_relation_service.go`), batch relation loading (`memo_service_converter.go`).

### 1h. User stats — `user_service_stats.go`

`GetUserStats` / `ListAllUserStats` apply the same VisibilityList / filter scoping as `ListMemos` before aggregating counts.

### 1i. In-app notifications — `user_service_notifications.go`

```302:316:/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/user_service_notifications.go
func canViewerAccessMemo(viewer *store.User, memo *store.Memo) bool {
	// admin bypass; PRIVATE → creator; PROTECTED → any authed user; PUBLIC → all
}
```

Filters comment/mention notification payloads so users never see memo content they cannot access.

